.TH S226-HR 1 2026-10-09 "s226" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
s226-hr \- live heart-rate display for the S226 fitness watch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s226-hr
.RB [ \-c
.IR selector ]
.RB [ \-a
.IR address ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-connect ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RI [ "Qt options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B s226-hr
connects to an S226 (H-Band / Veepoo) fitness watch over Bluetooth Low
Energy.
The main window is organised as tabs for the different areas of the
watch; the toolbar always holds controller selection, watch address,
Connect and the log panel.
.PP
The
.B Live
tab shows the heart rate as a large number that scales with the window,
today's step count and walking cadence in steps per minute (spm), and a
graph of heart rate and cadence over a selectable time span.
Optionally a metronome clicks along with the heart rate.
A blood-pressure measurement can be started from the Live tab.
.PP
The watch ends a heart-rate measurement on its own after 30 to 50
seconds; the program restarts it automatically.
When the watch goes out of range it keeps scanning and reconnects.
To make the watch connectable, wake it by pressing its button.
.PP
By default the program connects to the first watch that advertises as
S226.
With several watches around, pick one in the
.B Watch
field of the toolbar: it lists the watches connected to before, and
accepts an address typed in.
A watch shows the last two bytes of its address.
.PP
The cadence is measured between the moments the watch's step counter
changes, so it follows the watch's own update rate.
It reads 0 once the counter stops changing.
The status bar shows the watch's battery charge; its tooltip shows the
firmware version.
.PP
Further tabs (enabled only while connected) expose the rest of the
watch: settings, alarms, notifications, activity history and sport-mode
workouts.
See
.B TABS
below.
.PP
The program does not use BlueZ.
It drives a USB Bluetooth controller directly over raw HCI and detaches
the kernel's
.B btusb
driver from that controller while it runs, so the corresponding
.B hciN
adapter disappears until the program exits.
On combined WiFi/Bluetooth chips only the Bluetooth interface is
detached; WiFi keeps working.
.B bluetoothd
does not need to be stopped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-controller " " \fIselector\fR
Use this USB Bluetooth controller.
See
.B CONTROLLER SELECTION
below.
Without this option the controller chosen in the toolbar last time is
used, or the first available one.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-address " " \fIaddress\fR
Only connect to the watch with this Bluetooth address, written as
.IR XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX .
Without this option the watch chosen in the toolbar last time is used;
by default any watch advertising as S226.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-connect
Do not connect automatically on start.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fullscreen
Start in full-screen mode.
.TP
.B \-\-multi\-instance
Allow more than one running instance (for example to talk to two
watches on two controllers at once).
Without this option a second start raises the existing window and
exits.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.PP
The standard Qt options, such as
.BI \-platform " name"
and
.BI \-style " name",
are also accepted.
.SH CONTROLLER SELECTION
A controller
.I selector
is one of:
.TP
.B auto
The first controller the user may open (default).
.TP
.I N
The
.IR N th
controller as listed by
.BR "s226-cli \-\-list" ,
counting from 0.
.TP
.IB vvvv : pppp
USB vendor and product ID in hexadecimal, e.g.\&
.BR 0bda:b82c .
A
.B usb:
prefix, as used by Bumble, is accepted.
.TP
.I bus\-port.port
USB port path as in
.IR /sys/bus/usb/devices ,
e.g.\&
.BR 1\-10.1 .
This stays the same when the dongle is replugged into the same port.
.TP
.IB bus / device
Bus and device number as printed by
.BR lsusb (8),
e.g.\&
.BR 001/012 .
.TP
.BI hci N
The kernel adapter currently backed by that controller.
.PP
Controllers are recognised by their Bluetooth HCI USB interface
(class e0, subclass 01, protocol 01), not by their name.
.SH TABS
.TP
.B Live
Heart rate, steps, cadence, graph, metronome and blood-pressure control.
Readings are logged to a daily CSV file (see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.B Settings
Read and write the watch configuration: sedentary reminder, heart-rate
alarm, screen-on time, brightness, countdown preset, watch face, personal
data, feature toggles (metric, 24h, auto-HR, stopwatch, and so on) and
which message types the watch displays.
Use
.B Refresh
to load current values and
.B Apply
to write them.
.TP
.B Alarms
List the alarms stored on the watch; add, edit or delete entries.
.TP
.B Notify
Send a text message to the watch (choose the message type), show an
incoming-call screen with a caller name, or push
.B now-playing
metadata (title, artist, album, play state, volume).
Media keys pressed on the watch (next, play-pause, previous) are shown
in the tab. With
.B Forward watch media keys to system player
enabled,
those keys control the active MPRIS player on the session bus.
The
.B From player
button fills title/artist/album from that player.
With
.B Push system track changes to the watch
enabled, metadata is
sent to the watch whenever the active player changes track or play state.
With
.B Forward desktop notifications to the watch
enabled, session-bus
notifications (org.freedesktop.Notifications) are shown on the watch
as message type
.BR other .
Enable the
.B music
feature under Settings if the watch ignores metadata.
.TP
.B History
Fetch the watch's 5-minute activity slots for today or a previous day
(steps, distance, calories, activity value, average heart rate).
.TP
.B Sleep
Fetch sleep sessions for last night or a previous day (fall-asleep /
wake times, deep and light minutes, quality, wakes, stage curve).
.TP
.B Workouts
Fetch sport-mode sessions stored on the watch, with per-minute detail.
.SH SYSTEM TRAY
When a system tray is available, closing the window hides the application
to the tray instead of quitting.
The tray icon tooltip shows the connection state and the latest heart rate.
Left-click or choose
.B Show window
to restore the window;
.B Quit
in the tray menu (or
.BR Ctrl+Q )
exits fully and releases the Bluetooth controller.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B F11
Toggle full screen.
.TP
.B Esc
Leave full screen.
.TP
.B M
Toggle the metronome.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Show or hide the log panel.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/s226/s226\-hr/s226\-hr\-YYYY\-MM\-DD.csv
One file per day with every reading, columns
.BR time , " bpm" " and " spm .
Each row holds one reading; the other column is empty.
The graph is refilled from the last two hours of these files on start.
.TP
.I ~/.config/s226/s226\-hr.conf
Settings: selected controller and watch, watches connected to before,
metronome, volume, graph time span and window geometry.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70\-s226\-bluetooth.rules
udev rule that gives the logged-in user access to USB Bluetooth
controllers (the installation prefix may differ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory of the log files (default
.IR ~/.local/share ).
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory of the settings file (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.TP
.BR QT_FFMPEG_DECODING_HW_DEVICE_TYPES ", " QT_FFMPEG_ENCODING_HW_DEVICE_TYPES
Unless already set, the program sets both to an empty list so that Qt
Multimedia, which is only used for the metronome click, does not probe
for hardware video codecs.
.SH NOTES
The user needs read and write access to the controller's device node
.IR /dev/bus/usb/BBB/DDD .
Install the udev rule above, or on NixOS add the package to
.BR services.udev.packages .
.PP
Realtek dongles need the patch firmware that the kernel loads when the
dongle is plugged in.
It survives the takeover by
.BR s226-hr .
If the log warns about unpatched firmware, replug the dongle.
.PP
The calorie and distance values the watch reports are its own
estimates and are not shown.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on normal exit; non-zero if the command line could not be parsed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s226-cli (1),
.BR lsusb (8),
.BR udev (7)
.PP
